# Build context is this directory (Backend/) for every service Dockerfile.

# SECURITY — never let local secrets into an image. Every service calls Env.TraversePath().Load()
# at startup, which walks UP the directory tree looking for a .env. If one were copied into the
# image it would be found and loaded, silently overriding the platform's environment variables with
# development credentials — a local database connection string and the dev JWT signing key baked
# into a production container.
# The **/ prefix matters: a bare `.env` matches only Backend/.env, not AuthService/.env.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Build output — stale local artifacts would be copied over the ones restored inside the image,
# and they are large enough to slow every build.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Not needed to compile, and keeps the context small.
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/*.user
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
